1
00:00:07,760 --> 00:00:11,140
Can you believe it's been five years since our first date?

2
00:00:11,140 --> 00:00:12,730
I know.

3
00:00:13,500 --> 00:00:18,040
Do you think I should start watching The Flash TV show?

4
00:00:22,020 --> 00:00:24,310
That's what you're thinking about?

5
00:00:24,310 --> 00:00:26,490
Well, one of the things.

6
00:00:26,950 --> 00:00:29,310
Are any of them me?

7
00:00:29,760 --> 00:00:31,030
Yes.

8
00:00:31,030 --> 00:00:34,310
I thought, "I can't decide if I should watch The Flash TV show.

9
00:00:34,310 --> 00:00:36,970
I know, I'll ask Amy."

10
00:00:38,480 --> 00:00:39,770
Anyway...

11
00:00:41,700 --> 00:00:43,160
What are you doing?

12
00:00:43,160 --> 00:00:46,170
You're right, you did kind of kill the mood.

13
00:00:46,600 --> 00:00:48,180
I didn't kill anything.

14
00:00:48,180 --> 00:00:51,350
You did, talking about your stupid TV show.

15
00:00:51,350 --> 00:00:52,770
Excuse me.

16
00:00:52,770 --> 00:00:55,690
Starting to watch a television show that might run for years

17
00:00:55,690 --> 00:00:57,750
isn't a decision to take lightly.

18
00:00:57,750 --> 00:01:00,880
I'm wrestling with a big commitment issue here.

19
00:01:01,290 --> 00:01:02,440
Really?

20
00:01:02,440 --> 00:01:05,240
That's the commitment issue you're wrestling with?

21
00:01:06,260 --> 00:01:07,280
Sheldon,

22
00:01:07,280 --> 00:01:08,760
do you understand the irony

23
00:01:08,760 --> 00:01:11,390
of your fixation on a man with super speed,

24
00:01:11,390 --> 00:01:13,890
while after five years all I can get out of you

25
00:01:13,890 --> 00:01:17,030
is a distracted make-out session on a couch?

26
00:01:18,130 --> 00:01:21,090
Irony's not really my strong suit.

27
00:01:21,510 --> 00:01:23,420
But I have been getting better with sarcasm,

28
00:01:23,420 --> 00:01:25,400
if you want to give that a try.

29
00:01:25,880 --> 00:01:28,490
Oh, sure, I'd love to.

30
00:01:29,880 --> 00:01:31,920
Whenever you're ready.

31
00:02:00,260 --> 00:02:01,160
I don't want to rush you,

32
00:02:01,160 --> 00:02:03,120
but I'm closing a little early tonight.

33
00:02:03,120 --> 00:02:05,010
Ooh. Hot date?

34
00:02:05,010 --> 00:02:07,280
Uh, no. I overheard Bernadette tell Howard

35
00:02:07,280 --> 00:02:08,410
she was making him a meat loaf,

36
00:02:08,410 --> 00:02:11,080
and you don't have to not ask me twice.

37
00:02:13,500 --> 00:02:15,470
If I stick a lightbulb on this,

38
00:02:15,470 --> 00:02:18,210
wouldn't it make a great lamp for my bedroom?

39
00:02:19,590 --> 00:02:21,420
You're kidding, right?

40
00:02:21,420 --> 00:02:23,840
Oh. Is this freaking you out?

41
00:02:23,840 --> 00:02:26,730
I guess I'm just more of a Pottery Barn,

42
00:02:26,730 --> 00:02:29,340
Crate and Barrel kind of guy.

43
00:02:29,530 --> 00:02:32,660
Maybe Pier 1 if I really want to cut loose.

44
00:02:33,180 --> 00:02:34,790
All right. Never mind.

45
00:02:34,790 --> 00:02:36,840
No, no, no. Hey, you should totally get it.

46
00:02:36,840 --> 00:02:38,340
In fact, I'll buy it for you.

47
00:02:38,340 --> 00:02:39,790
Sold!

48
00:02:42,540 --> 00:02:43,760
Raj, you don't have to do that.

49
00:02:43,760 --> 00:02:46,030
Too late! No returns!

50
00:02:48,990 --> 00:02:51,120
That was really intense.

51
00:02:51,120 --> 00:02:53,890
Well, now we know, next time we go to the farmers' market,

52
00:02:53,890 --> 00:02:57,840
the order is petting zoo first, then buy vegetables.

53
00:03:02,220 --> 00:03:04,730
Oh, good. You're here. I need your assistance.

54
00:03:04,730 --> 00:03:07,990
Can it wait until I put a Band-Aid on a goat bite?

55
00:03:09,280 --> 00:03:10,430
What happened?

56
00:03:10,430 --> 00:03:14,010
Your buddy got mugged by some baby farm animals.

57
00:03:14,690 --> 00:03:16,300
Been there.

58
00:03:17,080 --> 00:03:18,420
So what do you need help with?

59
00:03:18,420 --> 00:03:21,400
Amy's mad at me, and I'm not clear why.

60
00:03:21,400 --> 00:03:23,640
Okay. Were you talking before she got upset?

61
00:03:23,640 --> 00:03:26,240
- Yes. - That's probably it.

62
00:03:27,190 --> 00:03:28,600
What'd you say to her?

63
00:03:28,600 --> 00:03:30,460
Well, I just asked her if I should start watching

64
00:03:30,460 --> 00:03:32,280
the new Flash TV series.

65
00:03:32,280 --> 00:03:33,680
And that made her angry?

66
00:03:33,680 --> 00:03:35,100
Baffling, right?

67
00:03:35,100 --> 00:03:37,150
We were necking like a couple of hooligans

68
00:03:37,150 --> 00:03:39,470
under the school bleachers.

69
00:03:39,950 --> 00:03:41,950
I stopped so I could ask the question.

70
00:03:41,950 --> 00:03:45,950
Next thing I know, good-bye, kissy face. Hello, yelly face.

71
00:03:46,990 --> 00:03:48,410
Well, Sheldon, when you're kissing a girl,

72
00:03:48,410 --> 00:03:50,560
she expects the attention to be on her.

73
00:03:50,560 --> 00:03:52,120
It was. I asked her

74
00:03:52,120 --> 00:03:55,000
if she thought I should watch The Flash.

75
00:03:55,370 --> 00:03:57,640
Yeah. I'm tapping out. Leonard?

76
00:03:57,990 --> 00:04:00,640
I'm gonna guess that your main concern is the time commitment

77
00:04:00,640 --> 00:04:02,860
of watching an entire season of a new show.

78
00:04:02,860 --> 00:04:04,460
Oh, no, not just a season.

79
00:04:04,460 --> 00:04:06,520
If I'm in, I'm in for the whole run,

80
00:04:06,520 --> 00:04:09,180
even if the quality declines.

81
00:04:09,180 --> 00:04:12,710
I get it. Smallville almost wrecked you.

82
00:04:13,450 --> 00:04:14,480
Exactly.

83
00:04:14,480 --> 00:04:15,910
You know, I waited ten years

84
00:04:15,910 --> 00:04:19,120
to see a guy everyone knows can fly, fly.

85
00:04:19,590 --> 00:04:20,990
Wait, what is wrong with you two?

86
00:04:20,990 --> 00:04:23,200
He was talking about television during their date night.

87
00:04:23,200 --> 00:04:26,290
Oh, not just date night-- our fifth anniversary.

88
00:04:26,290 --> 00:04:28,370
Okay, see, that's even dumber than you wondering

89
00:04:28,370 --> 00:04:32,140
if being bitten by a goat would give you the powers of a goat.

90
00:04:34,090 --> 00:04:36,260
If that happens, don't make me wait ten years

91
00:04:36,260 --> 00:04:38,920
to watch you eat a tin can.

92
00:04:40,970 --> 00:04:43,880
You guys ever notice that Emily has a bit of a twisted side?

93
00:04:43,880 --> 00:04:45,640
You mean 'cause she has weird tattoos?

94
00:04:45,640 --> 00:04:48,670
No, because she wants to have sex with me in a graveyard.

95
00:04:51,520 --> 00:04:53,270
One more time?

96
00:04:53,840 --> 00:04:55,690
She and I were supposed to watch

97
00:04:55,690 --> 00:04:57,880
the new Avengers movie tonight, but it was sold out.

98
00:04:57,880 --> 00:04:59,400
So I said, "What else do you want to do?"

99
00:04:59,400 --> 00:05:00,970
She said, "Let's go to a cemetery

100
00:05:00,970 --> 00:05:03,740
and do it on somebody's grave."

101
00:05:04,320 --> 00:05:07,740
Like, a random person or somebody she knew?

102
00:05:08,840 --> 00:05:11,250
What difference does it make?

103
00:05:11,710 --> 00:05:14,830
Well, if it's her father's grave and they didn't get along,

104
00:05:14,830 --> 00:05:17,170
then you know she holds a grudge.

105
00:05:18,450 --> 00:05:20,990
The only issue is that everybody has their own thing.

106
00:05:20,990 --> 00:05:22,800
And as long as it's two consenting adults,

107
00:05:22,800 --> 00:05:24,520
I guess I don't see the harm in it.

108
00:05:24,520 --> 00:05:25,830
Well, what if it's one consenting adult

109
00:05:25,830 --> 00:05:27,490
and one adult who pretends to consent

110
00:05:27,490 --> 00:05:30,200
because he's afraid of being alone?

111
00:05:31,550 --> 00:05:32,760
Well, then I guess bring a blanket.

112
00:05:32,760 --> 00:05:35,040
The grass gets damp at night.

113
00:05:37,140 --> 00:05:38,230
I don't know, guys.

114
00:05:38,230 --> 00:05:40,550
Maybe this relationship isn't for me.

115
00:05:40,550 --> 00:05:42,230
Maybe I should break up with her.

116
00:05:42,570 --> 00:05:44,620
Right. You're gonna break up with a girl who has sex with you.

117
00:05:44,620 --> 00:05:46,370
Can you believe this guy?

118
00:05:48,100 --> 00:05:51,040
I think if Raj wants to break up with a girl, he can do it.

119
00:05:51,040 --> 00:05:53,160
How are you saying that with a straight face?

120
00:05:53,160 --> 00:05:55,120
I don't know.

121
00:05:56,470 --> 00:05:57,870
You guys are being jerks.

122
00:05:57,870 --> 00:06:00,080
Buddy, other than Jenny Craig,

123
00:06:00,080 --> 00:06:02,610
you've never broken up with a girl in your life.

124
00:06:03,030 --> 00:06:04,610
You're one to talk.

125
00:06:04,610 --> 00:06:06,090
You've been complaining about Stuart

126
00:06:06,090 --> 00:06:07,170
living here for the past year.

127
00:06:07,170 --> 00:06:08,540
I don't see you showing him the door.

128
00:06:08,540 --> 00:06:09,350
That's not the same thing.

129
00:06:09,350 --> 00:06:10,720
Emily's a person.

130
00:06:10,720 --> 00:06:12,750
Stuart's more like an infestation,

131
00:06:12,750 --> 00:06:14,840
something you spray for.

132
00:06:15,220 --> 00:06:17,430
Baloney, okay? You two are as afraid of

133
00:06:17,430 --> 00:06:19,900
hurting someone's feelings as I am.

134
00:06:19,900 --> 00:06:22,780
That's not true. We were just laughing right in your face.

135
00:06:25,310 --> 00:06:26,290
Thanks for cooking.

136
00:06:26,290 --> 00:06:27,200
My pleasure.

137
00:06:27,200 --> 00:06:29,680
- That carrot was delicious. - Yeah.

138
00:06:30,960 --> 00:06:34,020
I wish I'd fought harder for the rest of 'em.

139
00:06:37,420 --> 00:06:39,210
Still haven't heard from her?

140
00:06:39,210 --> 00:06:41,690
No, and I'm confused.

141
00:06:41,690 --> 00:06:43,780
It's been nearly 24 hours.

142
00:06:43,780 --> 00:06:47,120
Amy should have figured out she's wrong by now.

143
00:06:48,720 --> 00:06:49,900
Hey, I don't think she's wrong

144
00:06:49,900 --> 00:06:52,580
about you going too slow in the relationship.

145
00:06:52,580 --> 00:06:53,950
Too slow?

146
00:06:53,950 --> 00:06:55,260
Yeah, you've been going out for years.

147
00:06:55,260 --> 00:06:56,750
You haven't even slept together.

148
00:06:56,750 --> 00:06:59,980
That's right. It's called foreplay.

149
00:07:01,790 --> 00:07:03,180
And I could make the case

150
00:07:03,180 --> 00:07:05,970
that you two aren't moving forward in your relationship.

151
00:07:05,970 --> 00:07:08,690
Uh, hello.

152
00:07:09,560 --> 00:07:11,290
Hello.

153
00:07:15,930 --> 00:07:18,500
No. Sheldon, we're getting married.

154
00:07:18,500 --> 00:07:20,360
But you've been engaged for over a year now,

155
00:07:20,360 --> 00:07:22,030
and you don't even have a wedding date.

156
00:07:22,030 --> 00:07:24,690
Well, we will. We're just not in a rush.

157
00:07:24,690 --> 00:07:26,370
Okay.

158
00:07:28,170 --> 00:07:30,440
We're gonna set a date.

159
00:07:30,440 --> 00:07:32,230
Okay. If you say so.

160
00:07:32,230 --> 00:07:33,820
Yeah, it's just, things are good right now.

161
00:07:33,820 --> 00:07:34,460
Really good.

162
00:07:34,460 --> 00:07:35,510
I'm focusing on my job.

163
00:07:35,510 --> 00:07:36,700
And we've been busy with our paper.

164
00:07:36,700 --> 00:07:37,440
So busy.

165
00:07:37,440 --> 00:07:38,600
Yeah, we'll pick a date when we pick a date.

166
00:07:38,600 --> 00:07:39,980
Yeah.

167
00:07:40,440 --> 00:07:42,090
Okay.

168
00:07:43,200 --> 00:07:44,610
You know, I can see why Amy's mad at you.

169
00:07:44,610 --> 00:07:47,380
Yeah, shut up, Sheldon!

170
00:07:49,990 --> 00:07:51,960
Did you eat all my yogurt?

171
00:07:51,960 --> 00:07:53,610
You mean the one that makes ladies do the thing

172
00:07:53,610 --> 00:07:54,770
that ladies pretend they don't do

173
00:07:54,770 --> 00:07:57,290
even though they do?

174
00:07:59,980 --> 00:08:01,290
You know...

175
00:08:01,290 --> 00:08:04,580
which yogurt I mean.

176
00:08:04,580 --> 00:08:07,720
I didn't touch it. Must have been Stuart.

177
00:08:08,200 --> 00:08:09,470
Maybe Raj is right.

178
00:08:09,470 --> 00:08:11,370
Maybe it's time we tell him he needs to move out.

179
00:08:11,370 --> 00:08:13,090
We should have done it months ago.

180
00:08:13,090 --> 00:08:15,330
I know, but his store was reopening,

181
00:08:15,330 --> 00:08:17,960
and then there were the holidays, and then he was sick.

182
00:08:17,960 --> 00:08:18,950
Yeah, right.

183
00:08:18,950 --> 00:08:21,350
Sick. He didn't have jaundice.

184
00:08:21,350 --> 00:08:24,160
He just looks like that.

185
00:08:29,580 --> 00:08:31,640
All right. Tonight's the night.

186
00:08:31,640 --> 00:08:32,400
Agreed.

187
00:08:32,400 --> 00:08:35,040
When he gets home, I'm dropping the hammer.

188
00:08:35,040 --> 00:08:36,880
Ooh, I like when you take charge.

189
00:08:36,880 --> 00:08:40,720
Oh, I'm not taking charge-- you're the hammer.

190
00:08:46,710 --> 00:08:47,920
So...

191
00:08:47,920 --> 00:08:49,970
why haven't we picked a date?

192
00:08:49,970 --> 00:08:50,860
You know why.

193
00:08:50,860 --> 00:08:52,370
Well, of course I know why.

194
00:08:52,370 --> 00:08:55,610
But just for fun... why?

195
00:08:55,720 --> 00:08:58,130
Not in a rush, busy with work...

196
00:08:58,130 --> 00:08:59,380
Things are good right now.

197
00:08:59,380 --> 00:09:01,100
Really good.

198
00:09:01,940 --> 00:09:03,630
You still want to get married, right?

199
00:09:03,630 --> 00:09:05,750
Oh, my God. Yes. Why would you even ask that?

200
00:09:05,750 --> 00:09:07,870
I don't know. Because we don't have a date?

201
00:09:07,870 --> 00:09:09,310
Well, you want a date, pick a date.

202
00:09:09,310 --> 00:09:10,780
It's not just the date.

203
00:09:10,780 --> 00:09:12,370
We haven't talked about anything.

204
00:09:12,370 --> 00:09:14,510
Big wedding, small wedding, indoor, outdoor...

205
00:09:14,510 --> 00:09:16,210
Outdoor? Oh.

206
00:09:16,210 --> 00:09:19,140
I can RSVP no right now.

207
00:09:20,080 --> 00:09:21,960
Okay, indoor it is. Big or small?

208
00:09:21,960 --> 00:09:22,910
Is your dad paying for it?

209
00:09:22,910 --> 00:09:23,570
I doubt it.

210
00:09:23,570 --> 00:09:25,550
Okay, two friends each.

211
00:09:27,490 --> 00:09:29,090
All right, well, I want it in a church.

212
00:09:29,090 --> 00:09:30,490
Fine. I want black-tie.

213
00:09:30,490 --> 00:09:32,050
Fine. I want to release butterflies.

214
00:09:32,050 --> 00:09:35,150
Seriously? Airborne worms?

215
00:09:36,470 --> 00:09:38,650
Okay. Well, then it's settled:

216
00:09:38,650 --> 00:09:41,270
small indoor church wedding, black-tie, no butterflies.

217
00:09:41,270 --> 00:09:43,170
- Sounds perfect. - Great.

218
00:09:44,730 --> 00:09:45,820
You still didn't pick a date.

219
00:09:45,820 --> 00:09:47,550
- Stay out of it! - Shut up!

220
00:09:54,350 --> 00:09:55,770
It's a beautiful night.

221
00:09:55,770 --> 00:09:58,060
Oh, yes, we've got the moon

222
00:09:58,060 --> 00:10:00,110
and the trees and...

223
00:10:00,110 --> 00:10:02,110
Elizabeth McNulty,

224
00:10:02,110 --> 00:10:05,660
who apparently died when she was the same age I am.

225
00:10:07,240 --> 00:10:09,510
Makes you feel alive, doesn't it?

226
00:10:09,510 --> 00:10:11,780
So does enjoying a meal at a well-lit restaurant,

227
00:10:11,780 --> 00:10:13,590
but here we are.

228
00:10:15,810 --> 00:10:17,750
You aren't scared, are you?

229
00:10:17,750 --> 00:10:19,770
Of ghosts, no.

230
00:10:19,770 --> 00:10:22,730
Of you, little bit.

231
00:10:25,290 --> 00:10:27,340
I'm sorry I've upset you.

232
00:10:27,340 --> 00:10:29,240
I shouldn't have asked so many questions.

233
00:10:29,240 --> 00:10:30,410
No, it's okay.

234
00:10:30,410 --> 00:10:33,670
Yeah, maybe it's good you got us talking about this stuff.

235
00:10:33,670 --> 00:10:35,590
Well, look at that--

236
00:10:35,590 --> 00:10:38,980
even when I'm causing problems, I make the world a better place.

237
00:10:39,570 --> 00:10:43,260
Hey, next, why don't we tackle your penchant for whining

238
00:10:43,260 --> 00:10:46,280
and Penny's love of the ol' glug-glug?

239
00:10:49,240 --> 00:10:51,090
Uh, Sheldon, I think we're good for now.

240
00:10:51,090 --> 00:10:52,650
Ah, well... very well.

241
00:10:52,650 --> 00:10:55,050
So does this mean you'll finally pick a wedding date?

242
00:10:55,050 --> 00:10:56,980
Here we go again.

243
00:10:56,980 --> 00:10:59,600
Why is everyone so concerned with us setting a date?

244
00:10:59,600 --> 00:11:01,530
We're committed to each other. We're happy.

245
00:11:01,530 --> 00:11:03,880
A ceremony isn't gonna change anything.

246
00:11:03,880 --> 00:11:06,140
So you're never getting married?

247
00:11:06,790 --> 00:11:09,280
It's his whining, isn't it?

248
00:11:09,280 --> 00:11:12,310
Sheldon, I'm not a whiner.

249
00:11:14,140 --> 00:11:17,350
It's amusing that he doesn't hear it.

250
00:11:18,100 --> 00:11:21,010
Look, all she's saying is we are in love

251
00:11:21,010 --> 00:11:23,440
so it doesn't matter if we get married tomorrow

252
00:11:23,440 --> 00:11:25,750
or a year from now or 50 years from now.

253
00:11:25,780 --> 00:11:28,050
Ew, 50? We'll be old and gross.

254
00:11:29,260 --> 00:11:31,510
Yeah, but we'll be old and gross together.

255
00:11:31,510 --> 00:11:35,060
My aunt and uncle were married 63 years.

256
00:11:35,060 --> 00:11:38,780
Towards the end, it was like watching cheese melt.

257
00:11:49,730 --> 00:11:52,110
Um... I'm free tonight.

258
00:11:57,390 --> 00:11:59,280
Are you saying you want to get married?

259
00:11:59,280 --> 00:12:02,510
Vegas isn't that far away.

260
00:12:03,070 --> 00:12:04,900
I'm in. Let's do it.

261
00:12:11,750 --> 00:12:14,360
After all these years.

262
00:12:14,360 --> 00:12:16,250
I'm really happy for the two of you.

263
00:12:16,250 --> 00:12:18,090
- Oh, thank you. - Thanks.

264
00:12:18,090 --> 00:12:20,410
Now get out of my spot.

265
00:12:23,810 --> 00:12:26,760
Bernie, Stuart just pulled up.

266
00:12:27,160 --> 00:12:28,070
So remember,

267
00:12:28,070 --> 00:12:30,060
the key is to be firm.

268
00:12:30,060 --> 00:12:31,110
Show no weakness.

269
00:12:31,110 --> 00:12:31,680
Right.

270
00:12:31,680 --> 00:12:33,060
Good luck.

271
00:12:33,670 --> 00:12:36,660
Howard Joel Wolowitz, you get back here.

272
00:12:37,960 --> 00:12:40,560
Never should have told you my middle name.

273
00:12:40,560 --> 00:12:41,540
Hey, guys.

274
00:12:41,540 --> 00:12:43,900
Hey, you got a minute?

275
00:12:43,900 --> 00:12:46,200
Sure. Uh, let me just put this stuff in the fridge.

276
00:12:46,200 --> 00:12:48,900
I felt bad for finishing your yogurt, so I bought more.

277
00:12:48,900 --> 00:12:51,210
And, Howard, your favorite fruit is in season.

278
00:12:51,210 --> 00:12:53,300
Crunch Berries.

279
00:12:55,000 --> 00:12:56,430
Don't let that sway you.

280
00:12:56,430 --> 00:12:57,470
It's hard not to.

281
00:12:57,470 --> 00:12:59,650
They taste so much better than real berries.

282
00:13:01,860 --> 00:13:02,750
What's up?

283
00:13:03,260 --> 00:13:06,030
So... we need to talk.

284
00:13:09,330 --> 00:13:11,220
You okay?

285
00:13:12,030 --> 00:13:14,530
I think we should talk.

286
00:13:14,880 --> 00:13:17,190
Is everything okay?

287
00:13:17,190 --> 00:13:19,850
Well... you've been living here a while now.

288
00:13:19,850 --> 00:13:22,740
I know. I may sell comic books at work,

289
00:13:22,740 --> 00:13:24,260
but the real superheroes

290
00:13:24,260 --> 00:13:26,630
are sitting right in front of me.

291
00:13:29,070 --> 00:13:31,780
Yeah...

292
00:13:31,780 --> 00:13:34,270
His middle name is David. Go.

293
00:13:36,010 --> 00:13:38,180
Look, I care about you a lot,

294
00:13:38,180 --> 00:13:41,740
but we are very different people.

295
00:13:41,740 --> 00:13:44,390
Are you breaking up with me?

296
00:13:44,390 --> 00:13:46,560
No, no, I'm just pointing out that

297
00:13:46,560 --> 00:13:50,350
you're dark on the inside and I'm dark on the outside.

298
00:13:51,650 --> 00:13:54,780
So, anyway, what I'm trying to say is...

299
00:13:56,720 --> 00:13:58,000
You need to take that?

300
00:13:58,000 --> 00:13:59,150
It's just my dad, probably calling

301
00:13:59,150 --> 00:14:01,660
to wish me a happy birthday.

302
00:14:02,370 --> 00:14:03,900
I'll call him back.

303
00:14:04,400 --> 00:14:06,900
You were saying?

304
00:14:07,420 --> 00:14:10,720
Look, Raj, be honest with me.

305
00:14:10,720 --> 00:14:12,350
If you want to end things, just do it.

306
00:14:12,350 --> 00:14:15,390
Don't expect me to do it for you.

307
00:14:15,810 --> 00:14:20,030
End things? I'm trying to tell you that I love you.

308
00:14:22,300 --> 00:14:28,740
* Happy birthday to you. *

309
00:14:36,330 --> 00:14:37,810
Wow, there's a Denny's in Vegas

310
00:14:37,810 --> 00:14:39,430
you can actually get married in.

311
00:14:39,870 --> 00:14:41,440
Doesn't sound very romantic.

312
00:14:41,440 --> 00:14:43,840
Yeah, but we could get heart-shaped pancakes.

313
00:14:44,400 --> 00:14:46,120
I'm sure we'll find a decent chapel.

314
00:14:46,120 --> 00:14:47,230
Yeah.

315
00:14:48,260 --> 00:14:50,330
- This is crazy! - I know!

316
00:14:51,570 --> 00:14:52,970
You think people are gonna be mad?

317
00:14:52,970 --> 00:14:55,740
Maybe. But this isn't about them; it's about us.

318
00:14:55,740 --> 00:14:58,630
It is. It is about us.

319
00:14:58,630 --> 00:15:00,040
And you know what the best part is?

320
00:15:00,040 --> 00:15:01,940
We took our time.

321
00:15:01,940 --> 00:15:04,800
I mean, we met, we were friends for a couple years,

322
00:15:04,800 --> 00:15:08,310
then we got together, and then we got untogether,

323
00:15:08,310 --> 00:15:09,890
then we worked out all our problems,

324
00:15:09,890 --> 00:15:12,230
and now we know everything about each other,

325
00:15:12,230 --> 00:15:14,100
we can just go forward

326
00:15:14,100 --> 00:15:16,140
with no surprises and no regrets.

327
00:15:16,140 --> 00:15:18,620
Right. No surprises.

328
00:15:20,020 --> 00:15:22,950
And no regrets.

329
00:15:27,620 --> 00:15:31,500
Uh, well, there-there's one thing

330
00:15:31,500 --> 00:15:33,650
I feel I should tell you.

331
00:15:33,650 --> 00:15:34,920
What?

332
00:15:35,430 --> 00:15:37,230
You know, so we can go into this

333
00:15:37,230 --> 00:15:39,420
with no secrets between us.

334
00:15:39,420 --> 00:15:41,050
What?

335
00:15:44,680 --> 00:15:46,550
Remember, uh, a couple years back

336
00:15:46,550 --> 00:15:49,360
when I was on that research ship in the North Sea?

337
00:15:49,360 --> 00:15:50,530
Yeah.

338
00:15:50,530 --> 00:15:53,350
Okay, well, there-there was a lot of drinking

339
00:15:53,350 --> 00:15:54,820
and craziness going on...

340
00:15:54,820 --> 00:15:55,610
No, you told me.

341
00:15:55,610 --> 00:15:58,360
Okay, um...

342
00:15:59,120 --> 00:16:02,020
Well, there was this girl.

343
00:16:02,540 --> 00:16:03,380
What did you do?

344
00:16:03,380 --> 00:16:04,740
Nothing...

345
00:16:05,460 --> 00:16:06,170
really.

346
00:16:06,170 --> 00:16:08,010
It was just kissing.

347
00:16:08,010 --> 00:16:08,900
And then what?

348
00:16:08,900 --> 00:16:10,480
And then nothing.

349
00:16:10,480 --> 00:16:12,420
I stopped it.

350
00:16:12,420 --> 00:16:16,680
But it still bothers me, and...

351
00:16:18,080 --> 00:16:20,850
I wanted you to know.

352
00:16:23,670 --> 00:16:25,900
All right.

353
00:16:27,940 --> 00:16:29,590
Did you ever do anything like this since we've been...?

354
00:16:29,590 --> 00:16:30,420
Nope, never.

355
00:16:30,420 --> 00:16:32,630
Oh, that's too bad.

356
00:16:34,130 --> 00:16:35,590
You know, can I ask you a question?

357
00:16:36,380 --> 00:16:38,300
Why are you telling me this now?

358
00:16:38,300 --> 00:16:41,400
Well, like I said, we're about to get married,

359
00:16:41,400 --> 00:16:44,090
and I-I want a clean slate.

360
00:16:44,090 --> 00:16:45,290
No secrets.

361
00:16:45,290 --> 00:16:46,840
Really? Be-Because to me,

362
00:16:46,840 --> 00:16:47,960
it seems like we're about to get married

363
00:16:47,960 --> 00:16:49,650
and you're trying to sabotage it.

364
00:16:49,650 --> 00:16:51,470
W-Would you rather I didn't tell you?

365
00:16:51,470 --> 00:16:53,280
No, I don't want there to be secrets between us.

366
00:16:53,280 --> 00:16:54,470
See, now I'm confused.

367
00:16:54,470 --> 00:16:55,980
I mean, what-what am I supposed to do?

368
00:16:55,980 --> 00:16:58,640
Uh, keep your mouth off other women.

369
00:16:59,860 --> 00:17:01,160
I can do that.

370
00:17:01,160 --> 00:17:01,580
Uh, uh, f-from now on,

371
00:17:01,580 --> 00:17:05,370
this mouth-- you and food, that's it.

372
00:17:08,750 --> 00:17:10,200
Okay.

373
00:17:11,000 --> 00:17:13,060
Yeah?

374
00:17:13,980 --> 00:17:16,320
Look, I'm not happy this happened,

375
00:17:16,320 --> 00:17:18,770
but I think I can get past it.

376
00:17:18,770 --> 00:17:20,570
I mean, we weren't engaged at the time,

377
00:17:20,570 --> 00:17:22,450
and it was just kissing.

378
00:17:22,450 --> 00:17:23,900
Right.

379
00:17:23,900 --> 00:17:25,580
Just kissing.

380
00:17:25,580 --> 00:17:27,420
It wasn't even very good.

381
00:17:27,420 --> 00:17:29,440
She was a smoker. I'd just been seasick...

382
00:17:29,440 --> 00:17:31,900
Okay, that's enough. Stop talking.

383
00:17:35,440 --> 00:17:36,880
So...

384
00:17:38,230 --> 00:17:40,030
we're still getting married?

385
00:17:41,670 --> 00:17:43,450
Yes.

386
00:17:44,580 --> 00:17:46,760
Because we love each other.

387
00:17:46,760 --> 00:17:48,120
Yes.

388
00:17:48,400 --> 00:17:50,930
And it's the happiest day of our lives.

389
00:17:51,300 --> 00:17:53,050
Don't push it.

390
00:18:02,200 --> 00:18:03,330
Hello.

391
00:18:03,330 --> 00:18:04,360
Hello.

392
00:18:04,360 --> 00:18:08,970
Listen, I've been thinking a lot about relationships

393
00:18:08,970 --> 00:18:11,650
and how difficult they can be, and I think...

394
00:18:11,650 --> 00:18:14,560
I've been thinking about them, too, Sheldon.

395
00:18:15,190 --> 00:18:18,780
Being your girlfriend is so challenging.

396
00:18:18,780 --> 00:18:20,410
Emotionally,

397
00:18:20,410 --> 00:18:21,770
physically.

398
00:18:21,770 --> 00:18:26,300
I've been incredibly patient for years.

399
00:18:26,300 --> 00:18:27,990
Strongly disagree.

400
00:18:27,990 --> 00:18:29,870
Go on.

401
00:18:30,390 --> 00:18:32,920
Okay, well...

402
00:18:33,690 --> 00:18:37,380
this isn't easy to say, because I love you,

403
00:18:37,380 --> 00:18:38,820
but...

404
00:18:39,930 --> 00:18:43,020
I need some time to take a step back

405
00:18:43,020 --> 00:18:46,360
and reevaluate our situation.

406
00:18:49,820 --> 00:18:53,140
I hope you understand.

407
00:18:55,080 --> 00:18:57,640
Okay.

408
00:18:58,030 --> 00:19:01,070
Bye, Sheldon.

409
00:19:18,160 --> 00:19:20,100
Well, Gollum...

410
00:19:22,110 --> 00:19:24,240
...you're an expert on rings.

411
00:19:25,680 --> 00:19:28,830
What do I do with this one?

